load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A reflection: the map that flips a space across a hyperplane mirror, fixing the mirror and reversing the perpendicular
# direction, an involution (applying it twice returns the start). Reflections are the generators of the Coxeter and Weyl
# groups, and reflecting a single 24-cell across its faces forever is exactly how the mesh tiles hyperbolic four-space.
# The form carries the vector space the reflection acts on.
form reflection
  link space, like vector-space
